<title>JAPAN: Mazda to double 98/99 new grad recruitment.</title>
<headline>Mazda to double 98/99 new grad recruitment.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mazda Motor Corp said on Friday it is planning to hire 520 new high school and college graduates in Japan in April 1998, nearly doubled from a planned 264 in April 1997.</p>
<p>The higher recuitment of new graduates for 1998/99 was to strengthen development in technology and products, Mazda said.</p>
<p>In addition, an increase in the number of employees retired or reaching retirement age is seen as rising in the mid- and long-term.</p>
<p>Of the 1998/99 recruitment, a total 410 new high school and college grads will be hired for development and production, up from a planned 170 in 1997/98.</p>
</text>
